{"1-4":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":3}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0770","lemma":"ἀσθενέω","tr":"astheneō","gloss":"be weak: weak","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":33},{"base":"G0235","lemma":"ἀλλά","tr":"alla","gloss":"but","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":638},{"base":"G1537","lemma":"ἐκ","tr":"ek","gloss":"out from","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":913},{"base":"G1411","lemma":"δύναμις","tr":"dunamis","gloss":"power","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":119},{"base":"G2198","lemma":"ζάω","tr":"zaō","gloss":"to live","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":139},{"base":"G4258","lemma":"προαμαρτάνω","tr":"proamartanō","gloss":"to sin beforehand","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G1414","lemma":"δυνατέω","tr":"dunateō","gloss":"be able","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4302","lemma":"προλέγω","tr":"prolegō","gloss":"to foretell","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G2064","lemma":"ἔρχομαι","tr":"erchomai","gloss":"to come","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":631},{"base":"G0548","lemma":"ἄπειμι","tr":"apeimi","gloss":"be away","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"MAT","chapter":18,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"But if he will not listen, take one or two others along, so that ‘every matter may be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.’","from":1},{"book":"DEU","chapter":19,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"A lone witness is not sufficient to establish any wrongdoing or sin against a man, regardless of what offense he may have committed. A matter must be established by the testimony of two or three witnesses.","from":1},{"book":"1PE","chapter":3,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"For Christ also suffered for sins once for all, the righteous for the unrighteous, to bring you to God. He was put to death in the body but made alive in the Spirit,","from":4},{"book":"DEU","chapter":17,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"On the testimony of two or three witnesses a man shall be put to death, but he shall not be executed on the testimony of a lone witness.","from":1},{"book":"MAT","chapter":10,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"For it will not be you speaking, but the Spirit of your Father speaking through you.","from":3},{"book":"JHN","chapter":8,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Even in your own Law it is written that the testimony of two men is valid.","from":1},{"book":"JHN","chapter":8,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"I am One who testifies about Myself, and the Father, who sent Me, also testifies about Me.”","from":1},{"book":"ROM","chapter":6,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"We were therefore buried with Him through baptism into death, in order that, just as Christ was raised from the dead through the glory of the Father, we too may walk in newness of life.","from":4}],"notes":[{"id":"deut-19-15-two-witnesses","title":"Every matter established by two or three witnesses","kind":"quotation"}],"groups":[]},"5-10":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":5}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G0096","lemma":"ἀδόκιμος","tr":"adokimos","gloss":"failing","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":8},{"base":"G2172","lemma":"εὔχομαι","tr":"euchomai","gloss":"to pray","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"G1438","lemma":"ἑαυτοῦ","tr":"heautou","gloss":"themself","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":322},{"base":"G2443","lemma":"ἵνα","tr":"hina","gloss":"in order that","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G0225","lemma":"ἀλήθεια","tr":"alētheia","gloss":"truth","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":109},{"base":"G0664","lemma":"ἀποτόμως","tr":"apotomōs","gloss":"severely","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2506","lemma":"καθαίρεσις","tr":"kathairesis","gloss":"destruction","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G2596","lemma":"κατά","tr":"kata","gloss":"according to","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":472},{"base":"G1487","lemma":"εἰ","tr":"ei","gloss":"if","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":508},{"base":"G4160","lemma":"ποιέω","tr":"poieō","gloss":"to do","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":569}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LAM","chapter":3,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":82,"source":"both","text":"Let us examine and test our ways, and turn back to the LORD.","from":5},{"book":"1CO","chapter":11,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":59,"source":"both","text":"Each one must examine himself before he eats of the bread and drinks of the cup.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":139,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":49,"source":"openbible","text":"Search me, O God, and know my heart; test me and know my concerns.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":139,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":49,"source":"openbible","text":"See if there is any offensive way in me; lead me in the way everlasting.","from":5},{"book":"1CO","chapter":9,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":46,"source":"openbible","text":"No, I discipline my body and make it my slave, so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified.","from":5},{"book":"REV","chapter":2,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":33,"source":"both","text":"Therefore, keep in mind how far you have fallen. Repent and perform the deeds you did at first. But if you do not repent, I will come to you and remove your lampstand from its place.","from":5},{"book":"GAL","chapter":6,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":31,"source":"both","text":"Each one should test his own work. Then he will have reason to boast in himself alone, and not in someone else.","from":5},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"See to it that no one falls short of the grace of God, and that no root of bitterness springs up to cause trouble and defile many.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"11-14":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"luke-g3065","name":"Luke","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"titus-g5103","name":"Titus","kind":"person","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"macedonia-g3109","name":"Macedonia","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"philippi-g5375","name":"Philippi","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"corinth-g2882","name":"Corinth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":14}],"words":[{"base":"G0040","lemma":"ἅγιος","tr":"hagios","gloss":"holy","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":222},{"base":"G0782","lemma":"ἀσπάζομαι","tr":"aspazomai","gloss":"to pay respects to","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":60},{"base":"G0026","lemma":"ἀγάπη","tr":"agapē","gloss":"love","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":116},{"base":"G3326","lemma":"μετά","tr":"meta","gloss":"with","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":465},{"base":"G1514","lemma":"εἰρηνεύω","tr":"eirēneuō","gloss":"be at peace","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G5370","lemma":"φίλημα","tr":"philēma","gloss":"kiss","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"G2675","lemma":"καταρτίζω","tr":"katartizō","gloss":"to complete","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G3063","lemma":"λοιπόν","tr":"loipon","gloss":"henceforth","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"G2842","lemma":"κοινωνία","tr":"koinōnia","gloss":"participation","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"G5426","lemma":"φρονέω","tr":"phroneō","gloss":"to reason","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":26}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EPH","chapter":2,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":20,"source":"both","text":"And in Him you too are being built together into a dwelling place for God in His Spirit.","from":14},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":18,"source":"openbible","text":"Pursue peace with everyone, as well as holiness, without which no one will see the Lord.","from":11},{"book":"ROM","chapter":12,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Live in harmony with one another. Do not be proud, but associate with the lowly. Do not be conceited.","from":11},{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"I appeal to you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that all of you agree together, so that there may be no divisions among you and that you may be united in mind and conviction.","from":11},{"book":"ROM","chapter":15,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"The God of peace be with all of you. Amen.","from":11},{"book":"ROM","chapter":5,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"And hope does not disappoint us, because God has poured out His love into our hearts through the Holy Spirit, whom He has given us.","from":14},{"book":"ROM","chapter":16,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"The God of peace will soon crush Satan under your feet. The grace of our Lord Jesus Christ be with you.","from":14},{"book":"1CO","chapter":16,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"The grace of the Lord Jesus be with you.","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":3},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]}}